Split the planner goal entry into a formation-centre entry and a member entry.

The upstream formation callback always computes

    end_pt_ = swarm_central_pos_ + swarm_scale_ * swarm_relative_pts_[drone_id]

so the received position is a formation centre and every member adds its own
slot offset.  That is correct for a formation command and wrong for a command
that addresses one member (or asks a member to hold), where the received
position is the member's own world target and must be used as-is.  Sending a
hold position through the formation entry moves the member by one slot offset
instead of holding it.

Three further problems block a single-member command:

  * the goal topic is the hard-coded global /move_base_simple/goal, which every
    member subscribes to, so a command cannot be addressed to a subset;
  * SEQUENTIAL_START makes drone_id >= 1 wait for have_recv_pre_agent_, so a
    member with no predecessor trajectory is never planned at all;
  * the formation similarity cost is hard-wired on for the global-trajectory
    path.  A lone member then optimises against a degenerate swarm graph and is
    dragged towards a formation configuration instead of its own target
    (measured: a member commanded 1.5 m sideways flew to the origin).

This patch adds a parameterised goal topic (default unchanged), an optional
member entry that uses the received position directly, does not wait for a
predecessor and plans without the formation cost, and leaves the formation entry
behaviour untouched.  The upstream file is not modified in the repository; the
patch is applied at image build time.
